SUMMARY:Asheville Jewish Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Jewish Film Festival\, presented by the UNC Asheville Center for Jewish Studies\, features four films with Saturday evening and Sunday afternoon screenings throughout October and November. The festival opens with a reception on October 10. \nOpening Night Reception: Saturday\, October 10 at 5:30 p.m. — Mountain Suites\, Highsmith Student Union \nFilm Screenings: \n\n“Once Upon My Mother”: Saturday\, October 10 at 7 p.m. and Sunday\, October 11 at 2 p.m. — Highsmith Student Union\n“Sabbath Queen”: Saturday\, October 17 at 7 p.m. and Sunday\, October 18 at 2 p.m. — Mullen & James Humanities Hall — post-film discussion to follow for both showings\n“The Sea”: Saturday\, October 24 at 7 p.m. and Sunday\, October 25 at 2 p.m. — Mullen & James Humanities Hall — post-film discussion to follow for both showings\n“The Ring”: Saturday\, November 7 at 7 p.m. and Sunday\, November 8 at 2 p.m. — Mullen & James Humanities Hall — post-film discussion to follow for both showings\n\nFor tickets and more information\, visit ashevillejewishfilmfestival.org. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Accessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu. \nVisitor Parking\n\nAll visitors must adhere to the University’s parking policy. Please visit the UNC Asheville Visitor Parking Permit Registration site to acquire a visitor permit to park on campus.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/asheville-jewish-film-festival/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Asheville-Jewish-Film-Festival-Event-Calendar.png
END:VEVENT
