SUMMARY:In the Round: 3rd Biennial Outdoor Sculpture Competition
DESCRIPTION:Join the Department of Art & Art History for the opening reception of In the Round: 3rd Biennial Outdoor Sculpture Competition. Artist-in-Residence Ledelle Moe will judge selected works at the Owen Hall Sculpture Garden and Window Gallery. These works will be on display for the next two years. \nThe opening reception will also feature Moe’s installation in the Owen Hall Window Gallery. \nIn the Round and the Artists-in-Residence program are made possible through the generous support of the Windgate Charitable Foundation. \nThis event is free and open to the public. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Accessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu. \nVisitor Parking\n\nAll visitors must adhere to the University’s parking policy. Please visit the UNC Asheville Visitor Parking Permit Registration site to acquire a visitor permit to park on campus.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/in-the-round-3rd-biennial-outdoor-sculpture-competition/
